    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.hippatterns\n\n### Description\n\nWhen deleting the entire code in a buffer, an out of range error coming from this plugin appears.\n\n### Neovim version\n\nv0.10.0-dev-1400+gbc850ba2a\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Inside an empty lua file write the following code in the first (and only) line: `local foo = 0`.\r\n2. Return to normal mode, and delete the code with `Vd`.\r\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nFor there to be no errors when deleting text.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nThe following error appears:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1159\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/62502207/dd0fd788-e3d3-46cb-a434-d35a71947976\">\r\n",
